refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public boolStreamPollHandle::isValid
Checks whether the stream of the handle is still open and has not reached its end.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 Returns &true; if the stream is open and not at end-of-file, &false;
 otherwise.

  &reftitle.examples;

   StreamPollHandle::isValid example


<?php
[$reader, $writer] = stream_socket_pair(STREAM_PF_UNIX, STREAM_SOCK_STREAM, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP);

$handle = new StreamPollHandle($reader);
var_dump($handle->isValid());

// The other end is closed, so the stream reaches its end.
fclose($writer);
var_dump($handle->isValid());

fclose($reader);
var_dump($handle->isValid());


   &example.outputs;


bool(true)
bool(false)
bool(false)
